> How do I format a set of get URL arguments in python?
**assistant**:
> To format a set of GET URL arguments in Python, you can use the `urllib.parse` module, which provides tools to manipulate URLs. Here's a simple way to construct a query string from a dictionary of parameters:
> 
> ```python
> import urllib.parse
> 
> # A dictionary of your query parameters
> params = {
>     'param1': 'value1',
>     'param2': 'value2',
>     'param3': 'value3'
> }
> 
> # Encode the parameters into a query string
> query_string = urllib.parse.urlencode(params)
> 
> # Assuming you have a base URL
> base_url = 'https://example.com/api'
> 
> # Construct the full URL
> full_url = f'{base_url}?{query_string}'
> 
> print(full_url)
> ```
> 
> This code snippet will encode your parameters and generate a complete URL with the query string appended to the base URL. The `urlencode` function automatically handles character encoding, making sure your parameters are safe to use in a URL.
